# The build context is `./app`, so these paths are relative to it.

# Dependencies are reinstalled inside the image. Sending a host `node_modules`
# in is slower, and it would send the wrong thing anyway: a native module built
# against the host's Node and libc does not run in the image.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Tests are not shipped, but they should still not bloat the context upload on a
# machine that has been running them.
test/

# The real database, its WAL siblings, and the backups directory. None of it
# belongs in an image: it is per-install state, it is volume-mounted, and an
# image that embeds a developer's listings gets pushed to a registry.
data/
data-demo/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.partial

# A developer's real configuration must never end up baked into an image that
# somebody else pulls. `.env.example` is deliberately kept - it is documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Anything an agent or editor leaves behind
.agents/
.claude/
.cursor/
.cache/
coverage/
*.log